I found the likely cause: selecting only `SPEC.encrypt-entry` can filter the loop claim out of the circularity set, causing symbolic unrolling instead of reuse. I’m stopping that diagnostic run and will invoke the complete spec so the proved loop claim is available while the entry claim is discharged.
diff --git a/concrete_tests.py b/concrete_tests.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cbfc54f4b35c0e618fbbb15b7418104c23124a7e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/concrete_tests.py
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+def encrypt(s):
+    """Rotate every character four places through the lowercase alphabet."""
+    out = ""
+    c = ""
+    for c in s:
+        out += chr((ord(c) - 97 + 4) % 26 + 97)
+    return out
+
+
+assert encrypt("hi") == "lm"
+assert encrypt("asdfghjkl") == "ewhjklnop"
+assert encrypt("gf") == "kj"
+assert encrypt("et") == "ix"
+assert encrypt("") == ""
+assert encrypt("xyz") == "bcd"
