codex
Both validation mutations were rejected as required: the false empty-string result got exit 1 with a stuck residual containing the actual empty string, and the ROT5 body mutation got exit 1 with residual codepoint 102 (`"f"`) against the ROT4 requirement 101 (`"e"`). The identity audit also finds the translated `solution.mpy` function exactly once in the entry theorem. I’m packaging these exact positive and negative commands into the reproducible runner now.
